          "description": {
            "comment": "Guaruba guarouba is endemic to the Brazilian Amazon, with limited occurrence to the south of the Amazon River and east of the Madeira River. There is a modeling based on habitat loss that indicates a population decline of between 23% and 40% in three generations, involving past and future. In addition, analysis of habitat loss in three past generations indicated a population decline of between 30% and 50%. For these reasons, G. guarouba was categorized as Vulnerable (VU) A4cd. source: https://salve.icmbio.gov.br/",
